## Before You Apply — Import Existing Route Tables

The `oci_core_default_route_table` resources modify the **existing** default route
tables on your VM Cluster VCNs. Terraform must import them before applying, or it
will replace them and wipe any pre-existing routes.

```bash
terraform init

# Import primary VCN default route table
terraform import \
  module.primary.oci_core_default_route_table.cluster_rt \
  {{ primary_route_table_id or '<primary-default-rt-ocid>' }}

# Import DR VCN default route table
terraform import \
  module.dr.oci_core_default_route_table.cluster_rt \
  {{ standby_route_table_id or '<dr-default-rt-ocid>' }}
```

Then add any pre-existing route rules back into the `route_rules` blocks in
`modules/oci-dg-region/main.tf` before running `terraform apply`.

